    "id": "p3-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Parabolas can be used to find the product $ab$ of any two positive real numbers $a$ and $b$. Consider the graph of $y=x^2$. We have labelled the points $A(-a,a^2)$ and $B(b,b^2)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q10-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"curveBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"parabola distinguished from the chord and projection guides\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 3, p3-q10-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\coordinate (A) at (-1,1);\n\\coordinate (B) at (1.6,2.56);\n\\coordinate (I) at (0,1.6);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (-1.85,0)--(2.15,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,-0.15)--(0,3.45) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[curveBlue,line width=0.8pt,domain=-1.75:1.8,samples=100] plot (\\x,{\\x*\\x});\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (A)--(B);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (A)--(-1,0);\n\\draw[black,dashed,line width=0.4pt] (B)--(1.6,0);\n\\fill[black] (A) circle (1.5pt) node[above left] {$A(-a,a^2)$};\n\\fill[black] (B) circle (1.5pt) node[above right] {$B(b,b^2)$};\n\\fill[black] (I) circle (1.5pt);\n\\fill[black] (-1,0) circle (1.5pt) node[below] {$-a$};\n\\fill[black] (1.6,0) circle (1.5pt) node[below] {$b$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
