    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that line segment $AB$ intersects the $y$-axis at the point $(0,ab)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The $y$-intercept is $(0,ab)$.\n\nUse the gradient $b-a$ and substitute $x=0$ into the equation of $AB$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{b^2-a^2}{b-(-a)}\\\\m_{AB}&=\\frac{(b-a)(b+a)}{b+a}\\\\m_{AB}&=b-a.\\end{align*}$$\nThe line through $A(-a,a^2)$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}y-a^2&=(b-a)(x+a)\\\\y&=(b-a)(x+a)+a^2.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(b-a)a+a^2\\\\y&=ab.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-a<0<b$, this intercept lies on the segment $AB$. Hence the intersection is $(0,ab)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p3-q10-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "For all possible pairs of integers ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
